{"about_the_game":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>APHASIA:</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Aphasia is a journey into the mind of a man who has forgotten how to confront his past.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You awaken in places that feel familiar but shouldn't. A motionless playground, a house trapped in an endless loop, a factory where you once worked.\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each environment is a fragment of memory, a buried emotion, or a piece of life that has resurfaced as a nightmare. Childhood, adolescence, and adulthood are all connected by a <strong>sense of guilt</strong> that watches you, grows with you, and follows you without ever running away.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In Aphasia, you will explore dreamlike and unsettling worlds inspired by dreamcore and liminal horror.\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>You are not a hero.</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>But you can still change who you want to be from who you were before the coma.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Your choices matter:\u00a0</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Will you face the past or run from it once again? Will you seek peace or erase everything?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >With <strong>ten</strong> narrative-driven levels and <strong>4</strong> distinct endings, Aphasia tells an intimate, psychological, and relentless story in which horror does not scream \u2014 it watches and waits.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Gameplay and Key Features:</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Immersive first-person exploration</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Environmental interaction with objects, puzzles, and hidden clues</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Nonlinear narrative structure with multiple endings</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Moral choices that influence the story and the protagonist's psychology</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each choice reveals fragments of a buried past, leading to multiple endings\u2014tragic, ambiguous, or hopeful.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >All paths are bound by one truth: an hidden trauma that still haunts the protagonist\u2019s mind.</p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3846570?t=1774306862","background_raw":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3846570/f33f44945be4097565401c2f4ff2c4115538365c/page_bg_raw.jpg?t=1774306862","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3846570/3ed53bb635d7cb3565d836d1574475082fee9f89/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1774306862","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3846570/3ed53bb635d7cb3565d836d1574475082fee9f89/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1774306862","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Camera Comfort","id":67},{"description":"Custom Volume Controls","id":68},{"description":"Narrated Game Menus","id":71},{"description":"Subtitle Options","id":65},{"description":"Partial Controller Support","id":18},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"detailed_description":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>APHASIA:</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Aphasia is a journey into the mind of a man who has forgotten how to confront his past.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You awaken in places that feel familiar but shouldn't. A motionless playground, a house trapped in an endless loop, a factory where you once worked.\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each environment is a fragment of memory, a buried emotion, or a piece of life that has resurfaced as a nightmare. Childhood, adolescence, and adulthood are all connected by a <strong>sense of guilt</strong> that watches you, grows with you, and follows you without ever running away.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In Aphasia, you will explore dreamlike and unsettling worlds inspired by dreamcore and liminal horror.\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>You are not a hero.</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>But you can still change who you want to be from who you were before the coma.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Your choices matter:\u00a0</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Will you face the past or run from it once again? Will you seek peace or erase everything?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >With <strong>ten</strong> narrative-driven levels and <strong>4</strong> distinct endings, Aphasia tells an intimate, psychological, and relentless story in which horror does not scream \u2014 it watches and waits.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Gameplay and Key Features:</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Immersive first-person exploration</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Environmental interaction with objects, puzzles, and hidden clues</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Nonlinear narrative structure with multiple endings</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Moral choices that influence the story and the protagonist's psychology</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each choice reveals fragments of a buried past, leading to multiple endings\u2014tragic, ambiguous, or hopeful.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >All paths are bound by one truth: an hidden trauma that still haunts the protagonist\u2019s mind.</p>","developers":["TommyMamo"],"genres":[{"description":"Adventure","id":"25"},{"description":"Indie","id":"23"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3846570/d9f3485284f2e7e9f8c4d82fb150c70c6b98de56/header.jpg?t=1774306862","is_free":false,"linux_requirements":[],"mac_requirements":[],"movies":[{"dash_av1":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/38